## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Operational dependency**: The Mahalanobis-based selection requires that `extract_features.py` has already been run to produce `feature_matrix.parquet` with raster values sampled at all grid points — OR at the very least, at a dense candidate point cloud across the survey footprint. If the feature matrix only contains labelled points (deposits + barren holes), the candidate pool will be insufficient.
>
> **Proposed resolution**: `generate_pseudo_absences_dissimilar()` will generate a dense candidate grid (e.g., every 500 m across the raster footprint), sample all available reprojected rasters at those points, compute dissimilarity, and select the 125 most dissimilar. This is self-contained within `download_vms_labels.py`.

> [!WARNING]
> **Feature availability at label-generation time**: `download_vms_labels.py` runs *before* `extract_features.py` in the pipeline. The new function will need to sample rasters directly (using `rasterio`) from the reprojected raster directory, which requires `reproject_grids.py` to have been run first. The script will check for raster availability and fall back to the old geographic method with a warning if no rasters are found.

