## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Stratification preference**: Should the 125 pseudo-absences be:
> - (a) The top-125 most dissimilar points globally (maximum dissimilarity, may cluster in one geological zone), OR
> - (b) Stratified by spatial block (e.g., top ~25 per spatial quadrant) to ensure geographic spread across the footprint while still being geologically dissimilar?
>
> **Recommendation**: Option (b) — stratified by spatial block — balances feature-space dissimilarity with spatial representativeness. The plan implements this as the default, with a flag to switch to pure top-K selection.

